  "result": {
    "summary": "The same frozen raw actor completed eight fixed fresh625 generic-greedy sessions. All 5000 hands passed captured-runtime, learned-logit argmax, terminal, server-counter, token-chain, and independent raw evidence review. Terminal ledger artifact registration was recovered in batches after a Windows command-length error; no session reran.",
    "conclusion": "Generic greedy execution improved the same checkpoint point estimate by 69.7938 bb/100 versus its separate sampled pilot and reached -9.4188 bb/100, close to historical Standard10 greedy. However the preregistered gate failed because the point remained negative and only 3/8 sessions were positive; uncertainty is large and neither CI excludes zero. Greedy is the correct current deployment direction, but this policy is not admitted to 20k or qualification.",
    "decision": "FRESH5K_TRANSFER_GATE_NOT_PASSED",
    "next_step": "Keep generic greedy as the deployment contract. Train a matched low-entropy actor-head treatment from Standard10 to test whether removing stochastic-entropy pressure sharpens learned action margins without imitation; gate first on untouched anchors and preserved Slumbot-state entropy/TV, then spend fresh hands only if it improves both mechanism and internal reward."
  },
